# Cursor Rules Index

Rules live in `.cursor/rules/`. `alwaysApply: true` rules are included in every agent session; others activate via `globs` when matching files are in context.

## Always applied

| Rule | Description |
|------|-------------|
| `chatwoot-core.mdc` | Core development principles and project conventions |
| `chatwoot-dev-commands.mdc` | Build, test, lint, and dev environment commands |
| `coding-standards.mdc` | Readability, naming, and code hygiene |
| `design-principles.mdc` | SOLID, composition, anti-patterns |
| `domain-application-layer.mdc` | Domain vs application vs transport boundaries |
| `fork-merge-conflicts.mdc` | Merge conflict avoidance for upstream sync |
| `fork-strategy.mdc` | Branch workflow — develop mirrors upstream, custom work on main |

## File-scoped (globs)

| Rule | Globs | Description |
|------|-------|-------------|
| `ruby-conventions.mdc` | `**/*.rb` | Ruby and Rails conventions |
| `vue-frontend.mdc` | `**/*.{vue,js}` | Vue 3 and JavaScript frontend |
| `tailwind-styling.mdc` | `**/*.vue` | Tailwind-only styling |
| `enterprise-edition.mdc` | `{app,enterprise,lib,config}/**/*.{rb,yml}` | Enterprise overlay rules |
